The decision rule — ask one question to select container
"What do I need to store, and what do I need to look up?"

----DONT MEMORIZE ANSWERS:::::-------------------
Your answer tells you the container directly:
Store value only, look up "does X exist?"     →  unordered_set
check uniqueness of frequencies               =  unoredered_set
Store value→index, look up "where is X?"      →  unordered_map
Store value→count, look up "how many X?"      →  unordered_map
Need sorted order                             →  map or set (ordered)
Need sequence, access by position             →  vector
Need fast front+back insert/delete            →  deque
LIFO (last in first out)                      →  stack
FIFO (first in first out)                     →  queue

